OK, this has happened to me once too often.  It is only until just recently
that we here were able to save games (alock.o problems, but that's another
issue).  I find now that when I restore a game, no matter how high my
hitpoints are, I get creamed by monsters within the first few moves of that
continued game.

When I want to save the game, typically I will do so just before I go down a
level.  Invariably when I restart the game, there are 10s of Mordor orcs,
owlbears, etc either in the same room where I start or in neighboring rooms to
which my pet(s) will alert me.  I was nailed today as a young valkyrie by an
owlbear which was present in the room with me when I reentered the game.  I
KNOW it wasn't there when I left the game, so what's the deal?  Needless to
say, I died an early death or I wouldn't be writing you good folk.  I'm a
relative novice but I know how to use what I have and to make use of those who
can help.  This hasn't happened just once or twice, either.  I know your luck
decreases by 1 each time you start the game, but I didn't realize that there
was a concomitant increase in likelihood of immediate death.  I also know, or
assume anyway, that this is not a typical problem or else everyone would be as
hopping angry as I am.  What gives?

